From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:24:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/29] Noah-MP combo: heat capacities per kg

combo multiplies cice and cwat (J m-3 K-1) by layer masses (kg m-2), and its
branches set T = tfrz or drop hfus*wliq without a phase change.

Use cice/denice and cwat/denh2o, and one enthalpy expression; phasechange
settles the phases. Both modules.

Effect measured with the combine fix (sensible heat when layers merge).

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
---
 .../Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmp_glacier.F90        | 13 ++++---------
 .../SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmplsm.F90  | 13 ++++---------
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmp_glacier.F90 b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmp_glacier.F90
index 25203d7f..b33fbde2 100644
--- a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmp_glacier.F90
+++ b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/module_sf_noahmp_glacier.F90
@@ -3135,17 +3135,12 @@ end if   ! opt_gla == 1
     dzc = dz+dz2
     wicec = (wice+wice2)
     wliqc = (wliq+wliq2)
-    h = (cice*wice+cwat*wliq) * (t-tfrz)+hfus*wliq
-    h2= (cice*wice2+cwat*wliq2) * (t2-tfrz)+hfus*wliq2
+    ! cb1: per-kg heat capacities (cice, cwat are per m3); phases kept, phasechange settles them
+    h = (cice/denice*wice+cwat/denh2o*wliq) * (t-tfrz)+hfus*wliq
+    h2= (cice/denice*wice2+cwat/denh2o*wliq2) * (t2-tfrz)+hfus*wliq2
 
     hc = h + h2
-    if(hc < 0.)then
-       tc = tfrz + hc/(cice*wicec + cwat*wliqc)
-    else if (hc.le.hfus*wliqc) then
-       tc = tfrz
-    else
-       tc = tfrz + (hc - hfus*wliqc) / (cice*wicec + cwat*wliqc)
-    end if
+    tc = tfrz + (hc - hfus*wliqc) / (cice/denice*wicec + cwat/denh2o*wliqc)
 
     dz = dzc
     wice = wicec
